            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CDBeck"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I found this recipe while looking for a way to use up the bumper crop of turnips I had this spring. Loved the peppery zip from the greens! For this recipe I chopped up fresh turnip greens, substituted a leek bulb for the onion (I needed to use the leek too!), and used balsamic vinegar because I didn't have tarragon. I also refrigerated the dip overnight to allow the flavors to blend. Next time I make this dip recipe I'll add red pepper flakes.",
